From c6a05b02e14d65142c0ba2e1e1af73bb1f81b259 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 19:00:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Part B: physical-N0 normalization + cell-average
 operator-convergence metric

Fixes the Part B diffusion validation harness per coag_validation_harness_fix
(scripts/figures only, no Fortran change):

- B1: use the physical N0 (and N0*m0 for additive) everywhere -- time mapping
  AND the analytic amplitude in _errors -- instead of the grid sums
  out["N0"]/out["M1"], which miss the ~9% of grains by number below the bottom
  bin edge and biased the analytic reference ~9% low. Applied in sweep(),
  bounded_report(), and dump_figure_data() (panels A and B).
- B2: add _cell_errors() -- relative L1 of the bin CONTENTS vs the exact solution
  integrated over the same geometric-mean bins. Zero for the exact IC by
  construction, so it isolates the coagulation operator rather than the
  piecewise-constant reconstruction floor that dominates cont_L1 (cont_L1 at t=0
  is 0.365 at ratio 2, ~90% of the evolved value). Mass-, area- (a^2), and
  number-weighted.
- B3: panelB.tsv gains cont_L1_t0 (the reconstruction floor) and cellL1_mass/
  area/number; panelB_distributions.tsv regenerated.
- B4: convergence panel now plots the cell-average error (mass solid, area
  dashed) with slope -1 and -2 references; cont_L1 and its t=0 floor are quoted
  in the text, not plotted. plot now renders headless (Agg) and writes png+pdf.
- A1: _run_nemo gains ic="bin"|"point" (bin default unchanged); "point" enables
  the Part C like-for-like comparison (Part C commit held pending a time-mapping
  decision).

Harness note: the panel-B cell-average dump uses nb_outputs=120 (was 40). At the
finest grids the cell-average is a tiny tail quantity and coarse output-time
sampling made the linear-in-time interpolation overestimate it ~20% at ratio
1.15; 120 snapshots converge it (0.017->0.014 mass, 0.011->0.009 area). cont_L1
is reconstruction-dominated and time-insensitive, so it is unchanged.

Regenerated panelB.tsv reproduces the fix-brief acceptance table to <=3.3% on
every value; cell-average monotone decreasing for both kernels.

